# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ariane133 + a real PDN — the vehicle for NDR shielding against STRAPS
#
# `specialnets_scope.md` §5(b).  On an imported design every routing layer is
# ALL-SIGNAL: a LEF states a wire's width and says nothing about which tracks
# a power grid takes, so the pattern carries no rails and NDR's credit / bond
# machinery has nothing to bite on.  The rails are in the DEF's SPECIALNETS
# and nowhere else, which is why this vehicle needs a POWER-ROUTED DEF.
#
# It is `ariane133_m4-m7.buda` with two additions and nothing else:
#   * the spliced strap DEF instead of the plain one, and
#   * an NDR rule that actually asks the questions (shield + credit + bond).
#
# WHY M4-M7 AND NOT THE FULL STACK: with all ten layers the interconnect
# lives on M8-M10 while the PDN stops at M7, so straps and signal metal
# occupy almost disjoint layers and every strap lookup returns "no rail" —
# the code would run, do nothing, and look fine.  Declaring seven layers with
# M6/M7 as TOP puts ~97% of the wire on the two layers carrying 1686 straps.
# Measured there: 304 of 305 M6 bit-wires and 668 of 668 M7 bit-wires
# span-overlap a strap, and 46 M6 + 26 M7 sit within ONE track pitch of one —
# which is the population R5a crediting is about.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The netlist and macro LEF are fetched (see ReadMe.md).  The strap DEF is
# GENERATED — it is `demo/ariane/ariane.def` with the SPECIALNETS of a pdngen
# run spliced in — so it cannot be checked in and the remedy has to be stated
# here rather than left to a reader complaining about a path.
require_file ariane.v fakeram45_256x16.lef hint Fetch them first:  python3 flow/ariane133/fetch.py   (~12 MB, checksum-pinned; see flow/ariane133/ReadMe.md)
require_file ariane_keepout.def hint Generate it:  see docs/internal/openroad_pdn_recipe.md (run pdn.tcl through OpenROAD for ariane_pdn.def, then splice its SPECIALNETS into demo/ariane/ariane.def per section 8.1)

open_bdb ariane133_ndr.bdb

set_import_scale dbu
set_unit_check on

corner_margin dx 3000 dy 3000
set_min_stub_length 1000

# `outside` tames the 13,034 OBS keepouts inside the macros; `stripes` is what
# makes the PDN affordable — its straps cross the die, so they are not inside
# any block and the `outside` rule cannot reach them.  Without it the Hanan
# grid goes ~6,327 -> ~3.2M cells and the planner does not finish.
set_keepout_loci outside stripes

def_layer 1 metal1 H LOW 30
def_layer 2 metal2 V LOW 30
def_layer 3 metal3 H LOW 30
def_layer 4 metal4 V LOW 30
def_layer 5 metal5 H LOW 30
def_layer 6 metal6 V TOP 30
def_layer 7 metal7 H TOP 30

# The DEF whose SPECIALNETS carry the power grid: 6673 strap wires, of which
# 1596 are on M6 and 90 on M7 — the layers this stack routes on.
import_def_lef ariane_keepout.def fakeram45_256x16.lef
import_verilog ariane.v

derive_container_bboxes margin 4000

# ── the rule ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A per-bus shield with BOTH opt-ins that need a rail to mean anything:
#   `credit` (R5a) — an END shield may be dropped when an identity-matching
#                    rail already runs beside the bus and spans it.
#   `bond`   (R6)  — an emitted shield is strapped to the grid wherever a
#                    matching rail crosses it on the adjacent perpendicular
#                    layer.  M6 is V and M7 is H, so they are exactly that
#                    pair for each other.
# Restricted to the strap-bearing TOP layers, and scoped rather than global:
# the question is whether a strap is SEEN, and governing every bundle would
# answer it while also re-planning the design around shield demand.
#
# THE SCOPE HAS TO BE A BUS THAT ROUTES.  This is a FLOORPLAN DEF: it places
# the 133 SRAMs and nothing else, so the 16 pure-logic containers have no
# placed descendant and every bundle between them has no geometry and no
# candidates.  `amo_req_o` — the widest bus in the design at 131 bits — is
# exactly that: driven by `ex_stage_i/lsu_i/i_store_unit/i_amo_buffer`, it
# can never be routed here, and a rule scoped to it governs a bundle that
# places nothing.  The nets with geometry are the SRAM-connected ones.
def_ndr pdn_shield shield bus net VDD credit bond layers metal6,metal7
set_ndr i_cache_subsystem/i_nbdcache/ pdn_shield
dump_ndr

# ── routing interface ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
derive_busterms 4

add_blocks_from_bdb 0
add_blocks_from_bdb 1 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 2 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 3 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 4 skip

# Rule attachment precedes bundling: the bundler splits a mixed-rule bundle
# into rule-uniform parts, so `set_ndr` above is what makes the governed bits
# arrive as their own bundle.
run_hier_bundler depth 4
generate_hier_topologies
run_planner hier 2
run_nuts
# The m4-m7 vehicle heals on both sides of DNUTS and this needs the same: a
# congested imported design reaches detailed placement with overlaps the
# abstract solve could not resolve, and without the repair 99 bit-wires land
# where ~980 do with it — measured, and nothing to do with the NDR rule (a
# control with the rule removed places the same 99).
negotiate_congestion
run_detailed_nuts
negotiate_congestion
check_design
report_wirelength
